<Project>

  <!--
    Properties that depend on whether a project is genuinely a test project.

    Why this file exists rather than Directory.Build.props:

      Directory.Build.props is imported BEFORE NuGet package props, so IsTestProject is
      not yet known there. Directory.Build.targets is imported AFTER, by which point
      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk has set IsTestProject=true on the projects that reference it.

      Keying these off the tests/ directory path instead marks support libraries such as
      MaintOrbit.TestUtilities as test assemblies. `dotnet test` then attempts to execute
      them and fails to locate testhost.dll, because a class library has no test host.

    The condition below is therefore a statement of fact — "this project references the
    test SDK" — rather than an assumption drawn from where the file happens to live.
  -->

  <!--
    CA1707 — "remove underscores from member name"

    docs/08-development/testing-strategy.md §4 mandates Method_Scenario_ExpectedResult for
    test names. The convention makes a failing test readable in CI output without opening
    the file. The analyzer rule targets public API surface, which a test assembly does not
    have.

    Scoped to real test projects deliberately. MaintOrbit.TestUtilities is an ordinary
    library whose members should follow ordinary naming, so it must not inherit this.
  -->
  <!--
    CA1848 — "use LoggerMessage delegates instead of ILogger.LogInformation"

    A performance rule about allocation on high-throughput logging paths. It is right about
    production code and irrelevant here: a test that exercises the logging pipeline logs
    once, and rewriting that single call as a source-generated delegate would obscure what
    the test is actually asserting.

    Scoped to test projects only, so the rule keeps applying to every path that runs under
    load. Application code must still use LoggerMessage.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(IsTestProject)' == 'true'" Label="TestProjects">
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1707;CA1848</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
